WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.665
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:08.061
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.361 --> 00:00:15.066
Unit thirty-five: Upper-Intermediate Champion!. In this unit, you will review B2 and celebrate your progress.

4
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:16.970
mastery.

5
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.424
mastery means great skill or knowledge in something.

6
00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:23.176
She showed real mastery of English grammar.

7
00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:25.890
Your turn. Say: mastery.

8
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.731
mastery.

9
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:31.764
proficiency.

10
00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:34.917
proficiency means a high level of ability.

11
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:37.913
The certificate shows your English proficiency.

12
00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:40.975
Your turn. Say: proficiency.

13
00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:44.804
proficiency.

14
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:46.841
eloquence.

15
00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:51.352
eloquence means speaking clearly, beautifully and persuasively.

16
00:00:51.652 --> 00:00:53.651
Nita spoke with great eloquence.

17
00:00:54.351 --> 00:00:56.562
Your turn. Say: eloquence.

18
00:00:59.262 --> 00:01:00.345
eloquence.

19
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.270
articulate.

20
00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.003
articulate means able to express ideas clearly.

21
00:01:06.303 --> 00:01:08.836
He's articulate in both Khmer and English.

22
00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.759
Your turn. Say: articulate.

23
00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:15.588
articulate.

24
00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:18.130
critical analysis.

25
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.850
critical analysis means carefully examining ideas and evidence.

26
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.695
The essay requires critical analysis.

27
00:01:26.395 --> 00:01:29.663
Your turn. Say: critical analysis.

28
00:01:32.363 --> 00:01:33.921
critical analysis.

29
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.034
debate skills.

30
00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:40.161
debate skills means the ability to argue clearly in a discussion.

31
00:01:40.461 --> 00:01:42.496
Her debate skills won the competition.

32
00:01:43.196 --> 00:01:46.022
Your turn. Say: debate skills.

33
00:01:48.722 --> 00:01:49.956
debate skills.

34
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.056
advanced level.

35
00:01:52.756 --> 00:01:55.963
advanced level means the level after upper-intermediate (C1).

36
00:01:56.263 --> 00:01:59.063
Next term, Nita will start the advanced level.

37
00:01:59.763 --> 00:02:02.114
Your turn. Say: advanced level.

38
00:02:04.814 --> 00:02:06.012
advanced level.

39
00:02:07.017 --> 00:02:08.331
final presentation.

40
00:02:09.031 --> 00:02:13.271
final presentation means the last talk you give at the end of a course.

41
00:02:13.571 --> 00:02:16.070
Her final presentation was about tourism.

42
00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.655
Your turn. Say: final presentation.

43
00:02:22.355 --> 00:02:24.076
final presentation.

44
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:27.036
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:30.848
Congratulations, Nita! You've completed Online Upper-Intermediate.

46
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.452
Thank you! Never have I learned so much in one year.

47
00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.620
Your final presentation was extremely articulate.

48
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:43.369
What helped me most was the debate practice.

49
00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:48.250
If you hadn't worked so hard, you wouldn't be ready for the advanced level.

50
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.411
I'm about to start it next month. I can't wait!

51
00:02:53.717 --> 00:02:56.494
Grammar focus: B2 grammar review.

52
00:02:56.794 --> 00:02:58.585
Let's review the B2 grammar.

53
00:02:58.885 --> 00:03:05.435
Perfect and continuous tenses, mixed and third conditionals, inversion, cleft sentences, passives and modals.

54
00:03:05.735 --> 00:03:09.558
For example: If I hadn't practised, I wouldn't be so fluent now.

55
00:03:09.858 --> 00:03:13.935
Keep using these structures in your speaking and writing to reach advanced level.

56
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.136
Now read and listen. From Intermediate to Advanced.

57
00:03:18.436 --> 00:03:23.199
When Nita started Upper-Intermediate, she could communicate, but not always precisely.

58
00:03:24.483 --> 00:03:28.909
Over thirty-five units, she developed critical analysis and debate skills.

59
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:34.550
Never had she spoken with such eloquence as in her final presentation.

60
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.755
What impressed her teachers most was her growing confidence.

61
00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:44.290
She is now about to begin the advanced level, ready for new challenges.

62
00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:47.899
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:48.199 --> 00:03:50.222
A high level of ability is blank.

64
00:03:50.522 --> 00:03:54.674
A, proficiency. B, eloquence. C, debate skills.

65
00:03:58.683 --> 00:04:00.927
The answer is A: proficiency.

66
00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:04.625
By 2030, I blank my degree.

67
00:04:04.925 --> 00:04:08.439
A, will have finished. B, will finish. C, finished.

68
00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.577
The answer is A: will have finished.

69
00:04:16.083 --> 00:04:18.164
Never blank such a great speech.

70
00:04:18.464 --> 00:04:21.688
A, I have heard. B, have I heard. C, I heard.

71
00:04:25.683 --> 00:04:27.404
The answer is B: have I heard.

72
00:04:28.917 --> 00:04:31.439
Able to express ideas clearly is blank.

73
00:04:31.739 --> 00:04:35.334
A, articulate. B, mastery. C, advanced level.

74
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.024
The answer is A: articulate.

75
00:04:42.517 --> 00:04:46.211
According to the text, what impressed Nita's teachers most?

76
00:04:46.511 --> 00:04:51.244
A, her accent. B, her growing confidence. C, her vocabulary.

77
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:58.190
The answer is B: her growing confidence.

78
00:04:59.683 --> 00:05:03.659
Now it's your turn to speak. What will you do to keep improving your English?

79
00:05:08.959 --> 00:05:16.755
What I'll do is read every day, join debates and watch films without subtitles. By next year, I'll have reached advanced level.

80
00:05:17.055 --> 00:05:18.729
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:19.717 --> 00:05:23.716
Great work today! You learned eight new words and b2 grammar review.

82
00:05:24.016 --> 00:05:27.632
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

83
00:05:27.932 --> 00:05:33.083
Congratulations! You have finished Online Upper-Intermediate. See you in Online Advanced!

84
00:05:33.383 --> 00:05:36.186
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

